# Backend Service Development Standards

> **Based on Auth Service Implementation Patterns**  
> This rule defines the complete development standards for all backend microservices in the Logistics Aggregator Portal, derived from the production-ready auth service implementation.

## **CRITICAL: Service Architecture Patterns**

### **Mandatory Service Structure**

Every backend service MUST follow this exact structure:

```
backend/service-name/
├── prisma/
│   ├── schema.prisma          # Database schema with audit patterns
│   └── migrations/            # Version-controlled migrations
├── src/ OR ./                 # Source code location
│   ├── controllers/           # Business logic handlers
│   ├── middleware/            # Service-specific middleware
│   ├── routes/                # API route definitions
│   ├── services/              # Business service layer
│   └── utils/                 # Service utilities
├── config/                    # Configuration modules
│   ├── database.js            # Prisma client setup
│   ├── redis.js               # Redis client setup
│   └── swagger.js             # OpenAPI documentation
├── .env.example               # Environment template
├── .env                       # Environment variables (auto-generated)
├── Dockerfile                 # Container configuration
├── package.json               # Dependencies and scripts
└── server.js                  # Entry point with Express setup
```

### **Database Schema Patterns (Prisma)**

**MANDATORY: Every service schema MUST include:**

```prisma
// Base audit fields for ALL models
model BaseModel {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@map("base_model")
}

// REQUIRED: Audit logging model for every service
model AuditLog {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId      String?  // User who performed action
  action      String   // CREATE, UPDATE, DELETE, etc.
  resource    String   // Table/model name
  resourceId  String?  // ID of affected resource
  changes     Json?    // What changed
  ipAddress   String?  // Request IP
  userAgent   String?  // Request user agent
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())

  @@map("audit_logs")
}

// Service-specific models follow this pattern
model ServiceEntity {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  // Service-specific fields
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  // Relationships
  auditLogs AuditLog[] @relation("EntityAuditLogs")

  @@map("service_entities")
}
```

**Database Naming Convention:**

- Service DB: `logistics_{service_name}` (e.g., `logistics_users`, `logistics_shipments`)
- Table names: snake_case with service prefix if needed
- Field names: camelCase in Prisma, snake_case in DB

## **Controller Implementation Patterns**

### **Standard Controller Structure**

Based on auth service patterns, every controller MUST follow:

```javascript
// controllers/entityController.js
const { PrismaClient } = require("@prisma/client");
const { getRedisClient } = require("../config/redis");
const prisma = new PrismaClient();

class EntityController {
  // MANDATORY: All methods must be static
  static async create(req, res) {
    try {
      // 1. Input validation (use Joi schemas)
      // 2. Business logic
      // 3. Database transaction
      // 4. Audit logging
      // 5. Response formatting

      const entity = await prisma.entity.create({
        data: validatedData,
        select: {
          // Only select needed fields for security
          id: true,
          name: true,
          createdAt: true,
        },
      });

      // MANDATORY: Audit logging
      await prisma.auditLog.create({
        data: {
          userId: req.user?.userId,
          action: "CREATE",
          resource: "Entity",
          resourceId: entity.id,
          changes: { created: validatedData },
          ipAddress: req.ip,
          userAgent: req.get("User-Agent"),
        },
      });

      res.status(201).json({
        status: "success",
        data: { entity },
      });
    } catch (error) {
      console.error("Entity creation error:", error);
      res.status(500).json({
        status: "error",
        message: "Internal server error",
        code: "INTERNAL_ERROR",
      });
    }
  }

  static async getById(req, res) {
    // Implementation pattern...
  }

  static async update(req, res) {
    // Implementation pattern...
  }

  static async delete(req, res) {
    // Implementation pattern...
  }

  static async list(req, res) {
    // Implementation with pagination...
  }
}

module.exports = EntityController;
```

